    "text": "",
    "title": "MYCC",
    "summary": "## MYCC (Mindmap Knowledge System)\n\nThe MYCC section covers the project's self-description document (`MYCC.md`) and the autonomous knowledge discovery system that compiles it into a structured, LLM-enriched knowledge tree called the **mindmap** — the primary memory and discovery mechanism for agents in the repository.\n\n### Architecture & Data Model\nThe mindmap is a tree of **Nodes** stored in `.mycc/mindmap.json`. Each Node has a slash-separated `id` path, original markdown `text`, extracted `title`, LLM-generated `summary`, `level`, `children`, and directional `links` (target_type: node/file/url/term). Two in-memory-only flags (never serialized) track origin: `is_mycc` (originates from MYCC.md) and `is_patch` (created/modified by a patch). These drive compile (only is_mycc nodes get summaries) and patch rebuild logic.\n\n### Compilation & Exploration\n`/mindmap compile` parses `MYCC.md` into sections (code-block-aware), builds the tree, and generates summaries using an **Explorer Agent** (`explorer-agent.ts`) with **A-N-C-E** context (Ancestors, Node, Child summaries, agent bEhavior). The explorer runs on `TriologueLite` (shared triologue submodules: store/compact/pending-tools/tp-fix) with per-message JSONL transcript persistence, auto-compaction at threshold, and a 25-round budget (force-stop at 5, steering hints appended to the last tool result). It uses 9 tools (`read_file`, `ls`, `grep`, `mark_file`, `web_search`, `web_fetch`, `mark_url`, `mark_term`, `final`); plain-text output is rejected (only `final` exits). Fallback: budget exhaustion triggers a tools-free retryChat over a minified transcript. Compilation is rotation-based (`.new`/`.bak`, temp+rename atomic save), lock-based resumption (4h freshness), pre-population from old tree (summary/links/text), and dependency-aware parallel summarization (semaphore, max 3 concurrent).\n\n### Patch System\nAgent-discovered knowledge is recorded as append-only patches in `.mycc/mindmap-patch.jsonl` (add/update/delete), hash-gated and validated (orphan-prevention: empty title/text or malformed parent path rejected at append/read/write/rebuild). Actions are replayed at load time via `applyPatchAction` (pure, no LLM; idempotent adds; `sanitizeLinks` filters malformed links so patch-added `term` links survive for recall's root \"Key Terms\" hoisting). `/mindmap compile` rebuilds patches (BFS dedup) and preserves MYCC.md-deleted nodes as `add` patches so trimmed content survives.\n\n### Agent Interface\nThe `recall` tool queries the tree by path, collecting hoisted terms at root and marking children `[M]` (MYCC.md-sourced) or `[P]` (patch-added). Each agent process has an independent mindmap instance (process isolation). Slash commands: `/mindmap compile|get|patch|validate|rebuild-patches`.\n\n### Key Files\n- `MYCC.md` — source of truth, compiled into the mindmap\n- `src/mindmap/types.ts` — Node, Link, Mindmap, ANCEContext, MindmapPatchAction\n- `src/mindmap/compile.ts` — rotation-based compilation, lock resumption, parallel summarization\n- `src/mindmap/explorer-agent.ts` — autonomous 9-tool explorer with 25-round budget\n- `src/mindmap/compile-utils.ts` — markdown parsing, node building, lock management\n- `src/mindmap/load.ts` — load JSON, set/strip in-memory flags\n- `src/mindmap/patch.ts` — cascading summary regeneration, node operations, applyPatchAction\n- `src/mindmap/patch-jsonl.ts` — append-only JSONL log, validatePatchAction, rebuildPatches\n- `src/mindmap/validate.ts` — hash-based validation\n- `src/mindmap/get-node.ts` — tree traversal utilities\n- `src/mindmap/diff-mindmap.ts` — diff_nodes, save_mindmap_atomic\n- `src/tools/recall.ts` — agent-facing query tool with [M]/[P] markers\n- `src/slashes/mindmap.ts` — slash command interface\n- `docs/mindmap-design.md`, `docs/mindmap-redesign.md`, `docs/mindmap-usage.md` — design docs and usage guide\n\n### Previously Marked Files\n- docs/mindmap-usage.md (User-facing usage guide for the mindmap system: slash commands, get_node tool, startup behavior, process isolation, wiki vs mindmap comparison, and best practices.)\n- MYCC.md (The authoritative source of truth and project self-description, compiled into the mindmap.)\n- src/mindmap/types.ts (Core type definitions: Node (id, text, title, summary, level, children, links, is_mycc/is_patch in-memory flags), Link (target_type: node/file/url/term), Mindmap, ANCEContext, MindmapPatchAction (add/update/delete with links field for patch-added term hoisting), CompileOptions.)\n- src/mindmap/compile.ts (Main compilation orchestration: rotation-based save (temp+backup), lock-based resumption (4h freshness), dependency-aware parallel summarization with semaphore (max 3 concurrent), pre-population from old tree.)\n- src/mindmap/explorer-agent.ts (Autonomous explorer agent loop with 9 tools (read_file, ls, grep, mark_file, web_search, web_fetch, mark_url, mark_term, final), 25-round budget, force-stop at 5 rounds, context compaction via LLM summarization + transcript save to disk.)\n- src/mindmap/compile-utils.ts (Utility functions: markdown parsing (code-block-aware), node building, link extraction, bottom-up collection, lock management (4h freshness), ProgressTracker.)\n- src/mindmap/load.ts (Load mindmap from JSON, set in-memory flags (is_mycc/is_patch), strip flags before serialization, default path resolution.)\n- src/mindmap/patch.ts (Cascading summary regeneration, node operations, applyPatchAction with link sanitization)\n- src/mindmap/patch-jsonl.ts (Append-only JSONL log, validatePatchAction, rebuildPatches)\n\n### Previously Marked URLs\n(none)\n\n### Previously Marked Terms\n- A-N-C-E (The summarization context model for mindmap nodes: A=Ancestor texts, N=Node text, C=Child summaries (pre-computed bottom-up), E=agent bEhavior context. Used by the explorer agent to generate enriched node summaries.)\n- is_mycc / is_patch flags (In-memory flags on mindmap nodes (never serialized): is_mycc=true means the node originates from MYCC.md (isomorph); is_patch=true means it was created/modified by a patch. Together they drive compile (only is_mycc nodes get summaries) and patch rebuild logic (is_patch on is_mycc → emit 'update' to preserve patched text).)",
    "level": 0,
