        "id": "/mycc.md",
        "text": "This file provides guidance for Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.",
        "title": "MYCC.md",
        "summary": "MYCC.md is the primary guidance document for Claude Code working in the mycc repository — a Node.js coding agent using Ollama (default) or DeepSeek API for LLM inference (embedding always via Ollama), with AgentContext as its central state container (ParentContext for main, ChildContext for child/IPC).\n\n**Architecture & Core Concepts**: State-machine agent loop (PROMPT/COLLECT/LLM/HOOK/TOOL/STOP/WAIT/SLASH states in `src/loop/states/`); Triologue now a thin facade over `src/loop/triologue/` modules (store, pending-tools, compact, wrap-up, checkpoint, tp-fix); AgentIO singleton (I/O, ESC/neglected mode, bang mode); IPC/IOC for main↔child; unified Loader (hot-reload, priority: built-in > project > user); Sequence, Confusion Index (hint rounds), mindmap (patch-JSONL knowledge tree), wiki (LanceDB), auto-claim, health-check.\n\n**Key Terminology**: tools/skills/hooks/routine distinctions; session/turn/chat hierarchy; PROMPT (loop stage) vs prompt (terminal component); autofly/streak momentum; checkpoint/recap; backlog (JSONL) vs livelog (in-memory) with TP constraint; hookish skills with `when` conditions compiled via LLM translation + jsep AST (no eval); Grant System intent language (VERB OBJECT PARAM... TO PURPOSE, with dangerous=i_know / batch=i_know escapes).\n\n**Team & Modes**: lead/teammate fork-based architecture, normal vs plan mode, todo/issue tracking with hash integrity, pinned todo reactivation, sealed-session principle, tool scope constraints (bg agents: bash/read/write/edit only).\n\n**WebUI** (`src/web/`, `src/serve/`): Vue 3 + WebSocket with steering, file uploads, teammate accordion UI, `/history` backed by triologue JSONL.\n\n**Development**: vitest, tmux/psmux interactive testing, ESLint with `no-console-in-tools` rule, debug flags (`--debug-tp/suggest/eval/prompt`), Docker, Windows/PowerShell notes, built-in skills table.\n\n**Pitfalls**: DeepSeek API limits, child agentIO constraints, Loop Notation (LN), tool-description best practices; reference docs in `docs/`.",
        "level": 1,
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "/mycc.md/project-overview",
            "text": "This project builds a tool called \"mycc\" -- A node.js coding agent implementation using Ollama (default) or DeepSeek API for LLM inference. The architecture follows a modular design with AgentContext as the central state container. Two API providers are supported: Ollama (full features including web_search, screen, read_picture) and DeepSeek (cloud-based, no web/screen tools but with prompt caching). Embedding for wiki/RAG always uses Ollama regardless of provider.",
            "title": "Project Overview",
            "summary": "The Project Overview section introduces **mycc** (v0.10.2), a Node.js coding agent using Ollama (default) or DeepSeek API for LLM inference. The architecture is modular with **AgentContext** (src/types.ts) as the central state container exposing modules: core, todo, mail, skill, issue, bg, team, wiki, and peer (peer discovery is a newer addition). Two implementations exist: ParentContext (lead, direct access) and ChildContext (teammates, IPC wrappers). Two API providers are supported: **Ollama** (default, full features: webSearch, webFetch, imgDescribe vision, screen/read_picture) and **DeepSeek** (cloud, no web/screen/vision but with prompt caching and thinking mode). Provider selection happens in `src/config.ts` via `getApiProvider()` reading the `API_PROVIDER` env var; `src/engine/chat-provider.ts` statically imports both providers and re-exports the active one at module load, including `forkChat` for prompt-cache-preserving side chats. The RAG embedding facade (`src/engine/rag-provider.ts`) always uses Ollama regardless of chat provider, auto-inferring the embeddinggemma vs nomic provider from `OLLAMA_EMBEDDING_MODEL` (default nomic-embed-text) via `getRagProvider()`, with NAMESPACE isolating LanceDB tables per model. Process architecture: Terminal → Coordinator (src/index.ts) → Lead (ParentContext) → Teammates (ChildContext).",
            "level": 2,
            "children": [],
