          },
          {
            "id": "/mycc.md/pitfalls",
            "text": "**Tool descriptions are for LLM awareness, not user-facing:** the `description` field is read by the LLM to understand what a tool does. It should NOT be user-facing documentation with verbose parameter explanations or step-by-step workflows. The description is about **what** the tool does, not **how** it does it internally. Implementation details (confirmation prompts, mail notifications) belong in code comments, not the description field. Keep it concise and LLM-oriented.\n\n**DeepSeek API pitfalls:** when using DeepSeek (API_PROVIDER=deepseek): no web/screen tools (`web_search`, `web_fetch`, `screen`, `read_picture` unavailable); DSML stripping (the letter-box strips internal DSML markup like `<ds_safety>`/`<ds_thinking>`); prompt caching (automatic for repeated prefixes); embedding still uses Ollama (wiki/RAG requires a local Ollama with `nomic-embed-text`); `tool_choice=\"none\"` for wrap-up mode (prevents raw XML tool calls). Detailed reference: `docs/deepseek-api-reference.md`.\n\n**agentIO singleton works differently in child processes:** `agentIO` (`src/loop/agent-io.ts`) is imported by both main and child, but `initMain()` is only called in the main process. `isMainProcess()` returns `true` in main (lead), `false` in child (teammates) — `isMainProcessFlag` defaults to `false` and only becomes `true` after `initMain()`. **Important**: only use `isMainProcess()` to distinguish lead vs teammate context. Other methods (`ask()`, `exec()`) throw in child processes. For code working in both contexts: use `agentIO.isMainProcess()` to check, `ctx.core.question()` for user questions (IPC), `ctx.core.brief()` for logging (IPC in child).\n\n**Loop Notation (LN):** a compact notation for message role rotation in the agent loop. Each comma-separated unit is one message. Units: `system` (system prompt), `user` (user query), `[tool1, tool2]?` (assistant's batched tool call, `?` = called by LLM), `tool1!` (tool result, one at a time), `agent` (assistant text reply), `_tool1_` (tool call replaced with placeholder after compaction). Example single-turn: `system, user, [tool1]?, tool1!, agent`. Example with batching + compaction: `system, user, [tool1]?, tool1!, [tool2, tool3]?, tool2!, _tool3_, agent, user, agent` (system → user → tool1 call → result → tool2+tool3 batched → tool2 result → tool3 compacted → agent reply → user → agent reply). Conventions: `[]?` groups batched calls from the same delta; `!` marks a result; `_` wraps a compacted call; bare units (system/user/agent) are pure text.",
            "title": "Pitfalls",
            "summary": "The \"Pitfalls\" section (MYCC.md, line 192) documents four gotchas:\n\n1. **Tool descriptions target the LLM, not users**: the `description` field is read by the LLM to know *what* a tool does — not verbose user-facing docs or workflow steps. Implementation details (confirmation prompts, mail notifications) belong in code comments.\n\n2. **DeepSeek API pitfalls** (API_PROVIDER=deepseek): no web/screen tools (`web_search`, `web_fetch`, `screen`, `read_picture`); DSML stripping (letter-box strips `<||DSML||...>` tags using U+FF5C fullwidth pipes via `stripInternalMarkup()` in `src/utils/letter-box.ts`); prompt caching is automatic for repeated prefixes; embedding still requires local Ollama with `nomic-embed-text`; `tool_choice=\"none\"` in wrap-up mode prevents raw XML tool calls. Six concrete API bugs (thinking/reasoning_effort conflict, arguments-as-JSON-string, required `type` field, reasoning_content echo, mode-switch gaps, DSML leaks) are detailed in `docs/deepseek-api-pitfalls.md`, fixed mainly in `src/engine/deepseek.ts` (`normalizeMessage()`, `retryChat`). Full API reference: `docs/deepseek-api-reference.md`.\n\n3. **agentIO singleton in child processes** (`src/loop/agent-io.ts`): imported by both main and child, but only `initMain()` (main/lead) sets `isMainProcessFlag = true`; it defaults to `false` in teammates. Only use `isMainProcess()` for lead/teammate detection — `ask()` throws `'question() only available in main process'` in children. Use `ctx.core.question()` (IPC) for questions and `ctx.core.brief()` (IPC) for logging.\n\n4. **Loop Notation (LN)**: compact notation for message role rotation — `system`/`user`/`agent` (text), `[tool1, tool2]?` (batched calls from one delta), `tool1!` (result, one at a time), `_tool1_` (compacted placeholder). Example: `system, user, [tool1]?, tool1!, agent`.",
            "level": 2,
            "children": [],
            "links": [
              {
                "target_type": "file",
                "file_path": "MYCC.md",
                "comment": "Pitfalls section source — defines tool description guidance, DeepSeek pitfalls, agentIO child-process behavior, and Loop Notation"
              },
              {
                "target_type": "file",
