              },
              {
                "target_type": "term",
                "term_name": "Loop Notation (LN)",
                "comment": "Compact notation for message role rotation in the agent loop: system/user/agent for text, [tool1, tool2]? for batched tool calls from one delta, tool1! for results, _tool1_ for compacted placeholders"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "/mycc.md/reference-documents",
            "text": "- `docs/agent-context.md` - AgentContext module (Chinese)\n- `docs/agent-loop.md` - Agent loop (Chinese)\n- `docs/agent-tools.md` - Built-in tools reference\n- `docs/child-context.md` - Child process and IPC (Chinese)\n- `docs/dynamic-loading.md` - Tool/skill loading mechanism\n- `docs/pinned-todo-reactivation.md` - Pinned todos and reactivation feature design\n- `docs/database-schema.md` - Data storage schema (Chinese, historical reference — SQLite removed in v0.7.0)",
            "title": "Reference Documents",
            "summary": "The \"Reference Documents\" section catalogs seven design/reference docs. **`docs/agent-context.md`** (Chinese) documents the AgentContext architecture: ParentContext (lead, direct module access) vs ChildContext (teammate, IPC forwarding), now with 9 modules — core, todo, mail, skill (Loader), issue, bg, team, wiki (LanceDB vector knowledge base), and peer (cross-instance discovery) — plus core features (question, imgDescribe, grants, confusion index, mode/auto control). Notably there is no `wt` module; worktrees are queried via `worktree-store.ts` functions. **`docs/agent-loop.md`** (Chinese) describes the STAR-principle agent loop, refactored into an explicit state machine (PROMPT→SLASH/COLLECT→LLM→HOOK→TOOL→STOP, plus WAIT for auto mode) with autoCompact (50K token threshold, runs in LLM state via forkChat for cache hits), COLLECT pre-collection pipeline (mails, hint rounds, todo nudging every 3 passes, brief nudging every 5), and team awaiting in STOP. **`docs/agent-tools.md`** is the built-in tools reference — 48 tools (v0.10.1) with scope constraints (main/child) across file ops, communication, issue/team management, background tasks, screen/image, todo, skill, wiki, mode control, checkpoint/recap, peers, and git_commit. **`docs/child-context.md`** (Chinese) covers child process IPC: IpcRegistry/IpcClient, WORK/IDLE/HOLDING/SHUTDOWN state machine, auto-claim of published issues (5s polling), and full message-type tables. **`docs/dynamic-loading.md`** documents the Loader class, three skill sources (user < project < built-in priority), hot-reload only for project `.mycc/` directories, and skill discovery via skill_search/skill_load. **`docs/pinned-todo-reactivation.md`** is a design doc for persistent pinned todos (main-only `todo_pinning` tool) and condition-based reactivation via forkChat on the nudge cadence. **`docs/archived/database-schema.md`** (Chinese, in `docs/archived/`) is historical — SQLite was removed in v0.7.0, replaced by in-memory `memory-store.ts` and JSON `worktree-store.ts`; it retains the old SQLite table definitions.",
